    "uri": "urn:oxidal:plugin:echo#mono",
    "name": "Oxidal Echo (Mono)",
    "category": "Delay",
    "comment": "Echo is eight kinds of delay behind one Mode control: Digital (clean), Tape (one sliding head with wow, flutter and wear), Heads (four heads on one loop), Bucket (bucket-brigade: darker as it gets longer, companded, a little noisy), Reverse (repeats play backwards), Duck (repeats drop while you play), Filter (a resonant sweep on the repeats) and Ping (as Digital in mono). Time sets the delay in milliseconds, or with Sync on, BPM and Division set it as a note value. Feedback is the number of repeats and goes a little past endless; Tone runs from dark through open to thin; Mod is wow and flutter, the Duck amount, the Filter depth or a gentle chorus; Age is tape wear and bucket noise; Heads and Spacing choose and place the heads in Heads mode; Mix runs from dry to repeats only and lets the tail ring out when turned down; Hold loops what is in the memory. Up to 4 s. No latency.",
