  {
    "uri": "urn:oxidal:plugin:moment#mono",
    "name": "Oxidal Moment (Mono)",
    "category": "Delay",
    "comment": "Moment catches what you just played and turns it into a moving texture. The loop half records all the time: Catch keeps the most recent audio as a loop. Tape plays it at another speed or backwards, Stretch spreads it into slow overlapping slices, and Touch sticks on a slice while you play. Overdub adds to the loop and Fade sets how much of it stays on each pass. The wet half is Smear (separate echoes to a wash), Delay or Slip (a sliding pitch shift), with Chance letting sound in only some of the time and Freeze holding it. Route sends the input, the loop or both through the wet half, and the wet half is recorded while Catch is off. Clock sets the working sample rate of everything: lower is longer, deeper and darker; Grit makes it stepped and aliased. No latency.",
